  "prompt": "/deep-research In 2022, which states who were in the top 5 for death rates related to heart disease, also had chronic lower respiratory diseases in their top 5 leading causes of death in 2022. Use data from the CDC.",
  "prompt_prefix": "/deep-research ",
  "instruction": "In 2022, which states who were in the top 5 for death rates related to heart disease, also had chronic lower respiratory diseases in their top 5 leading causes of death in 2022. Use data from the CDC.",
  "answer": "Based on the research from CDC data sources, here are the findings:\n\n## Top 5 States by Heart Disease Death Rate (2022, Age-Adjusted)\n\n| Rank | State | Age-Adjusted Rate per 100,000 |\n|------|-------|-------------------------------|\n| 1 | Oklahoma | 257.1 |\n| 2 | Mississippi | 248.0 |\n| 3 | Alabama | 234.2 |\n| 4 | Arkansas | 224.1 |\n| 5 | Louisiana | 224.0 |\n\n*Source: CDC WONDER Underlying Cause of Death database via KFF State Health Facts, ICD-10 codes I00-I09, I11, I13, I20-I51, age-adjusted to 2000 US standard population* [1]\n\n## CLRD in Top 5 Leading Causes of Death (2022)\n\nAccording to CDC NCHS \"Stats of the States\" data (cited by Becker's Oncology), CLRD (chronic lower respiratory diseases, ICD-10 J40-J47) appears in the top 5 leading causes of death for 44 of 51 jurisdictions. The only jurisdictions where CLRD is **not** in the top 5 are: California, District of Columbia, Hawaii, Minnesota, Texas, Utah, and Washington [2][3].\n\n## Intersection: All 5 Top Heart Disease States Have CLRD in Top 5\n\n| State | Heart Disease Rank | CLRD Rank in Leading Causes | Top 5 Causes (for verification) |\n|-------|-------------------|----------------------------|--------------------------------|\n| Oklahoma | 1 | 4 | Heart disease, Cancer, Accidents, **CLRD**, Stroke |\n| Mississippi | 2 | 3 | Heart disease, Cancer, **CLRD**, Accidents, Stroke |\n| Alabama | 3 | 4 | Heart disease, Cancer, Stroke, **CLRD**, Accidents |\n| Arkansas | 4 | 3 | Heart disease, Cancer, **CLRD**, Stroke, Accidents |\n| Louisiana | 5 | 5 | Heart disease, Cancer, Accidents, Stroke, **CLRD** |\n\n**All five states** that ranked in the top 5 for heart disease death rates in 2022 also had chronic lower respiratory diseases (CLRD) in their top 5 leading causes of death in 2022.\n\n## Sources\n\n[1] https://wonder.cdc.gov/ucd-icd10-expanded.html (CDC WONDER database; also cited by KFF at https://www.kff.org/state-health-policy-data/state-indicator/heart-disease-deaths-and-death-rates-per-100000-population)\n\n[2] https://www.beckersoncology.com/oncology/leading-causes-of-death-in-every-state-cdc (Becker's Oncology article citing CDC NCHS \"Stats of the States\" leading causes of death by state, 2022 data)\n\n[3] https://www.cdc.gov/nchs/state-stats/deaths/index.html (CDC NCHS Stats of the States - leading causes of death by state)",
  "answer_chars": 2311,
  "expected_answer": "Oklahoma, Mississippi, Arkansas",
